1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,555
Getting Ahead of Customer Concerns.

2
00:00:02,555 --> 00:00:08,152
There's a moment on every discovery call
when you'll ask the prospect to take the

3
00:00:08,152 --> 00:00:13,049
next step — fill out the application,
connect their bank account, share

4
00:00:13,049 --> 00:00:18,505
financial documents. How you frame that
ask determines whether concerns surface

5
00:00:18,505 --> 00:00:18,995
at all.

6
00:00:18,995 --> 00:00:24,370
Listen to this exchange between Andy
Murphy and a solo founder named Matthew

7
00:00:24,370 --> 00:00:24,800
Krick:

8
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:32,286
Matthew asks
what financial documents are needed. Andy

9
00:00:32,286 --> 00:00:39,587
separates the two paths: "If you wanted
something like a net seven or net 15, we

10
00:00:39,587 --> 00:00:46,981
typically do require 24 months of P&L and
balance sheet in monthly Excel format —

11
00:00:46,981 --> 00:00:54,282
they don't need to be audited. It could
just be management accounts or an export

12
00:00:54,282 --> 00:01:01,122
from your accounting software. And if you
just want Net-1, we don't require

13
00:01:01,122 --> 00:01:02,323
financials.".

14
00:01:02,323 --> 00:01:07,541
Matthew says he prepares his own books
and isn't comfortable sharing them since

15
00:01:07,541 --> 00:01:12,959
they're not professionally prepared. Andy
doesn't push: "That's perfectly fine. We

16
00:01:12,959 --> 00:01:17,843
have a very high success rate on our
Net-1. What we can always do is start

17
00:01:17,843 --> 00:01:23,262
with the Net-1. If you're able to get it
submitted by end of day tomorrow, I could

18
00:01:23,262 --> 00:01:28,145
have limits underwritten by Thursday and
we could do an onboarding call on

19
00:01:28,145 --> 00:01:28,747
Friday.".

20
00:01:28,747 --> 00:01:30,605
Matthew commits to Friday.

21
00:01:30,605 --> 00:01:33,206
Three things happen in that exchange.

22
00:01:33,206 --> 00:01:38,500
One: Andy separates Net-1 from float
before any concern can build.

23
00:01:38,500 --> 00:01:43,670
Two: He simplifies the financial
documents ask — "don't need to be

24
00:01:43,670 --> 00:01:46,534
audited, just management accounts.".

25
00:01:46,534 --> 00:01:52,506
And Three: When Matthew expresses
discomfort, he pivots to Net-1 with an

26
00:01:52,506 --> 00:01:54,104
immediate timeline.

27
00:01:54,104 --> 00:01:59,261
The prospect never felt pushed, and the
deal moved forward. Here are the three

28
00:01:59,261 --> 00:02:00,466
tactics behind it.

29
00:02:00,466 --> 00:02:03,624
**Tactic one: minimize the ask.**.

30
00:02:03,624 --> 00:02:08,217
When you describe the application
process, lead with how lightweight it is.

31
00:02:08,217 --> 00:02:10,265
Tim Jonas does this consistently:

32
00:02:10,265 --> 00:02:18,553
"For net one,
super simple, just need you to fill out

33
00:02:18,553 --> 00:02:26,634
the application, takes five, 10 minutes
and then email me your EIN document and

34
00:02:26,634 --> 00:02:33,161
articles of incorporation and that's
literally it for net one.".

35
00:02:33,161 --> 00:02:37,407
Dave Beddingfield adds something the
other AEs don't — he removes the

36
00:02:37,407 --> 00:02:38,594
commitment concern:

37
00:02:38,594 --> 00:02:47,412
"The
application takes 10 minutes, it's not a

38
00:02:47,412 --> 00:02:53,780
legal contract or binding you to any type
of spend.".

39
00:02:53,780 --> 00:02:58,433
Dave pairs the time investment with the
risk reduction on every call. The

40
00:02:58,433 --> 00:03:03,021
prospect hears: "This costs you 10
minutes and commits you to nothing.".

41
00:03:03,021 --> 00:03:06,550
**Tactic two: separate easy from hard.**.

42
00:03:06,550 --> 00:03:11,821
When float comes up, separate it from
Net-1 before the prospect has a chance to

43
00:03:11,821 --> 00:03:14,862
feel overwhelmed by the document
requirements.

44
00:03:14,862 --> 00:03:23,861
Andy Murphy on a call with Prenetics:
"We don't

45
00:03:23,861 --> 00:03:29,212
require financials for the net one
product.".

46
00:03:29,212 --> 00:03:34,178
The prospect hears "easy" before they
hear "documents." If Net-1 is all they

47
00:03:34,178 --> 00:03:39,606
need, the concern never surfaces. If they
want float, the heavier requirement comes

48
00:03:39,606 --> 00:03:44,241
after they're already engaged. And when
you do mention float documents,

49
00:03:44,241 --> 00:03:49,339
de-stigmatize them — "don't need to be
audited, just management accounts or an

50
00:03:49,339 --> 00:03:51,921
export from your accounting software.".

51
00:03:51,921 --> 00:03:55,218
**Tactic three: say it before they
ask.**.

52
00:03:55,218 --> 00:04:00,115
The concerns prospects have about
personal guarantees and credit checks

53
00:04:00,115 --> 00:04:05,712
don't go away just because you mentioned
them in your positioning. If you address

54
00:04:05,712 --> 00:04:11,028
them proactively when presenting the
application, the concern resolves before

55
00:04:11,028 --> 00:04:11,658
it forms.

56
00:04:11,658 --> 00:04:17,881
Cameron Baker does this on a call with
Healthycell — a deal that closed at

57
00:04:17,881 --> 00:04:18,392
$450K:

58
00:04:18,392 --> 00:04:27,415
Early in the
call, Cameron states: "The reason behind

59
00:04:27,415 --> 00:04:36,663
that is because we don't require any UCCs
or liens on the business or even personal

60
00:04:36,663 --> 00:04:38,129
guarantees.".

61
00:04:38,129 --> 00:04:44,808
Later, the prospect asks directly: "So,
no personal guarantees and no UCC?"

62
00:04:44,808 --> 00:04:49,321
Cameron confirms: "No personal guarantee.
No UCC.".

63
00:04:49,321 --> 00:04:55,295
Two words. The concern was already
handled — Cameron set it up earlier in

64
00:04:55,295 --> 00:05:01,767
the call. By the time the prospect asked,
it was a confirmation, not a concern.

65
00:05:01,767 --> 00:05:07,018
The through-line across all three
tactics: address the concern before it

66
00:05:07,018 --> 00:05:12,416
becomes one. Minimize the ask, separate
easy from hard, and say the things

67
00:05:12,416 --> 00:05:18,480
prospects worry about before they have to
ask. When you do this well, most concerns

68
00:05:18,480 --> 00:05:24,249
never surface — and the ones that do are
easier to handle. That's what the next

69
00:05:24,249 --> 00:05:25,358
section covers.
